# Review routing. GitHub requests a review from the owner of every path a pull
# request touches.
#
# There is one maintainer, so a catch-all would be enough to get the notification.
# The per-path entries below exist for a different reason: they make the trust
# boundary visible in the diff. A PR that touches only `website/` and a PR that
# touches `rust-core/crates/crypto` both get the same reviewer, but only the
# second one announces in its file list that it is changing code where a mistake
# is a vulnerability rather than a bug.
#
# Contributions are welcome everywhere — this routes review, it does not restrict
# who may open a PR. See CONTRIBUTING.md.

* @goduni

# ── The trust boundary ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Crypto primitives' composition, byte formats, and the key hierarchy. Frozen
# schemes here are pinned by golden vectors: a change that breaks one is a format
# break needing a new version, never an edit.
/rust-core/crates/crypto/     @goduni

# Keys never cross this boundary in plaintext — the invariant in CONTRIBUTING.md
# that cannot be relaxed by review.
/rust-core/crates/ffi/        @goduni
/rust-core/crates/keychain/   @goduni

# The client treats the transport as untrusted; this is the verify-before-apply
# path that enforces it.
/rust-core/crates/sync/       @goduni

# Encrypted-at-rest storage and the schema migrations that must keep old vaults
# readable.
/rust-core/crates/storage/    @goduni

# Real in-browser crypto, shipped to users as wasm.
/server-ui/crypto-wasm/       @goduni

# ── Supply chain ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These hold `contents: write`, `id-token: write`, and the signing secrets during
# a release. A change here can alter what users download without altering a line
# of product code.
/.github/workflows/           @goduni
/deny.toml                    @goduni

# ── The promises ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Security claims are part of the product. A change to what these documents
# promise is a change to what the project is accountable for.
/SECURITY.md                  @goduni
/THREAT_MODEL.md              @goduni
/CHANGELOG.md                 @goduni
